<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The shipping entitlements MINUS the M4 sync keys, for builds that cannot be signed
  with a real development certificate — CI, and any local `xcodebuild test`.

  Why this file exists (M4 T4, 2026-08-17): `com.apple.developer.icloud-*` are
  restricted entitlements, so macOS refuses to ad-hoc-sign a binary carrying them
  ("has entitlements that require signing with a development certificate") and there
  is no profile to fetch on a CI runner. The measured alternatives were both worse:
  `CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO` produces an UNSANDBOXED test host, which matters a great
  deal here because `RaconteTests` runs with the real app as its host — unsandboxed,
  `AppContainer.root()` resolves to the owner's actual `~/Library/Application
  Support/Raconte` instead of a throwaway container, and the launching app would scan
  and sweep his real archive. (It also breaks `BuildStampTests`, whose fixture paths
  only agree inside a container.)

  Keep in step with `project.yml`'s `targets.Raconte.entitlements.properties`: this
  file must be that list minus exactly the sync keys. `EntitlementsParityTests` fails
  if it drifts, so there is no need to remember.

  Used as `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS=Raconte/Raconte-nocloud.entitlements` on the
  xcodebuild command line; nothing in `project.yml` points at it, and no shipping build
  ever uses it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
